# Text is stored and checked out with LF on every platform, so builds and hashes match across the
# Windows, macOS and Linux runners. PowerShell scripts keep CRLF for Windows; binaries are never touched.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.glb binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.wasm binary
# Captured SSE frame logs are tracked with their CRLF bytes; the eol rule would rewrite them.
*-sse-frames.txt -text
